5 true] [17592186217431 1071 "![](images/93/9334b2ef84abbfc824ffd209a9a53482ff6c3d457b746e5f2e07722c916591a4.png)\n\nA chemist conducted several trials to measure the pH level of a new solution. Each trial produced one reading, and the histogram below summarizes the measured pH levels from the trials.\nWhat was the mean pH level measured across all trials?\n\n> A calculator is required to answer this question." 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217431 1072 #uuid "5150ff22-3db9-522a-ae1f-78c506e96b75" 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217431 1073 true 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217432 1068 #edb/ref 17592186214833 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217432 1069 "q-304398" 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217432 1071 "A music festival organizer is hiring $x$ musicians and $y$ stage managers for an upcoming event. The organizer must hire at least $15$ people in total, but wants to keep the total weekly pay at no more than $$12,000$. If each musician will be paid $$700$ per week and each stage manager will be paid $$950$ per week, and the organizer must hire at least $5$ musicians and at least $2$ stage managers, which of the following systems of inequalities represents this situation?" 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217432 1072 #uuid "e32218fa-677f-520d-b606-1e850d5dcfef" 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217433 1068 #edb/ref 17592186214839 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217433 1069 "q-304399" 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217433 1071 "A bakery is purchasing bags of flour and sugar from its supplier. The delivery truck can carry no more than $250$ pounds in a single shipment. Each bag of flour weighs $4.5$ pounds, and each bag of sugar weighs $6.8$ pounds. The bakery also wants to buy at least three times as many bags of flour as bags of sugar. Let $f$ represent the number of bags of flour and $s$ represent the number of bags of sugar, where $f$ and $s$ are nonnegative integers. Which of the following systems of inequalities best represents this situation?" 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217433 1072 #uuid "f18ee651-6809-5921-a06b-b0859960c296" 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217434 1068 #edb/ref 17592186214845 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217434 1068 #edb/ref 17592186214850 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217434 1068 #edb/ref 17592186214855 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217434 1068 #edb/ref 17592186214860 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217434 1069 "q-304404" 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217434 1071 "A film director is hiring $x$ camera operators and $y$ sound engineers for a movie project. The director must hire at least $18$ people in total, but wants to keep the total weekly pay at no more than $$24,000$. Each camera operator will be paid $$800$ per week, each sound engineer will be paid $$1,000$ per week, and the director must hire at least $6$ camera operators and at least $3$ sound engineers. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nThe system of inequalities that models this situation is the following:\n$800x + 1,000y \\le 24,000$ {{field-1}} {{field-2}} {{field-3}} {{field-4}}" 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217434 1072 #uuid "c20d88c9-3f7d-5c0a-93df-fda4b752a56f" 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217435 1068 #edb/ref 17592186214865 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217435 1069 "q-304798" 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217435 1071 "| $x$ | $d(x)$ |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $-3$ | $-6$ |\n| $1$ | $2$ |\n| $3$ | $0$ |\n\nThe table above shows three values of $x$ and their corresponding values of $d(x)$, where $d(x) = (r(x))/(x + 1)$ and $r$ is a linear function. What is the $y$-intercept of the graph of $y = r(x)$ in the $xy$-plane?" 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217435 1072 #uuid "9da964be-5f74-5218-9f2c-0b63743d3c59" 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217436 1068 #edb/ref 17592186214871 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217436 1069 "q-304800" 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217436 1071 "| $x$ | $z(x)$ |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $-6$ | $4$ |\n| $-4$ | $-2$ |\n| $-2$ | $0$ |\n\nThe table above shows three values of $x$ and their corresponding values of $z(x)$, where $z(x) = (v(x))/(x + 5)$ and $v$ is a linear function. What is the $y$-intercept of the graph of $y = v(x)$ in the $xy$-plane?" 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217436 1072 #uuid "706ee605-9478-5f4b-9d64-10720d139cfb" 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217437 1068 #edb/ref 17592186214877 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217437 1069 "q-305198" 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217437 1071 "A charity group is buying $k$ blankets and $m$ jackets for a donation drive. The group needs to purchase more than $60$ items in total, but wants to spend less than $$500$. If each blanket costs $$5$ and each jacket costs $$10$, which of the following systems of inequalities best models this situation?" 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217437 1072 #uuid "6baf7412-c614-5337-aed7-ed6f1fa8e96a" 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217438 1068 #edb/ref 17592186214883 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217438 1068 #edb/ref 17592186214888 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217438 1069 "q-305211" 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217438 1071 "A clothing manufacturer is buying $g$ jackets and $h$ hats for a shipment. The manufacturer needs to purchase more than $22$ items in total, but wants to spend less than $$400$. Each jacket costs $$18$ and each hat costs $$6$.\nSelect the correct options in the reasoning below.The system of inequalities that models this situation is the following:\n$18g + 6h < 22$ {{field-1}} {{field-2}}" 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217438 1072 #uuid "279a19f8-49a9-5775-b64c-4ed236781df2" 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217439 1068 #edb/ref 17592186214893 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217439 1068 #edb/ref 17592186214898 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217439 1069 "q-305231" 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217439 1071 "An office supplier is loading boxes of paper and toner cartridges onto a dolly. The dolly can carry no more than $160$ pounds. Each box of paper weighs $9.5$ pounds, and each box of toner weighs $11.2$ pounds. The number of toner boxes must be no more than the number of paper boxes. Let $p$ represent the number of paper boxes and $t$ represent the number of toner boxes, where $p$ and $t$ are nonnegative integers. Select the correct options in the reasoning below.The system of inequalities that models this situation is the following:\n$9.5p + 11.2t \\ge 160$ {{field-1}} {{field-2}}" 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217439 1072 #uuid "d4f12aa6-662e-5af9-9d9f-b4df2beeb6c5" 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217440 1068 #edb/ref 17592186214903 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217440 1069 "q-306034" 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217440 1071 "Dataset $A$: $10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10$\n\nDataset $B$: $10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 10, 15$\n\nTwo datasets, $A$ and $B$, are given above. Which of the following statements about the means and medians of the datasets is true?" 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217440 1072 #uuid "ef6c7b21-56b6-589e-9cac-76a09950a569" 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217441 1068 #edb/ref 17592186214909 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217441 1068 #edb/ref 17592186214913 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217441 1069 "q-306036" 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217441 1071 "The table shows the test scores, rounded to the nearest whole number, for a group of $50$ students.\n\n| Score | Number of Students |\n| --- | ---: |\n| $74$ | $5$ |\n| $76$ | $7$ |\n| $78$ | $10$ |\n| $80$ | $12$ |\n| $82$ | $9$ |\n| $84$ | $7$ |\n\nA new score of $100$ is added to the dataset, making $51$ scores in total. Which statement best compares the mean and median of the new dataset to those of the original dataset?\n\nThe mean of the new dataset is {{field-1}} the mean of the original dataset.\n\nThe median of the new dataset is {{field-2}} the median of the original dataset." 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217441 1072 #uuid "37a92cc5-af74-5e50-aa8c-e39445c8d6fc" 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217442 1068 #edb/ref 17592186214917 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217442 1069 "q-306041" 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217442 1071 "The ages, in years, of $20$ trees in a park were recorded, and the mean, median, range, and standard deviation were calculated. Later, it was discovered that the youngest tree’s age had been reported as $5$ years too high.\nWhich of the following statistics remains unchanged when recalculated using the corrected age?\n\n1. Mean\n2. Median\n3. Range\n4. Standard deviation" 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217442 1072 #uuid "026db7e3-76df-526c-8951-27764478d3e4" 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217443 1068 #edb/ref 17592186214923 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217443 1068 #edb/ref 17592186214927 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217443 1069 "q-306066" 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217443 1071 "The dataset $E$ is given by\n$10, 20, 30, 40, 50$\nand the dataset $F$ is given by\n$10, 20, 30, 40, x$\nwhere $x > 50$. Select the correct options in the following sentences.\nThe median of dataset $F$ is {{field-1}} the median of dataset $E$.\n\nThe mean of dataset $F$ is {{field-2}} the mean of dataset $E$." 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217443 1072 #uuid "1b456a89-a6f4-5648-b3e2-aea5cb3168bc" 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [17592186217444 1068 #edb/ref 17592186214931 13194139533378 17592186045585 true] [175921